[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "French Defence"]
[Variation "Advance Variation"]
[ECO "C02"]
[Character "positional,solid"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "c5-break,d4-pressure"]

1. e4 e6 { Prepares ...d5 and keeps a solid pawn on e6. The cost is that the bishop on c8 is hemmed in for now. } 2. d4 d5 { Challenges White's e4 pawn right away. }
3. e5 { White grabs space and cramps Black's kingside, but the pawn on e5 becomes a target. } 3... c5 { Attacks the base of White's pawn chain at d4. If d4 falls, the e5 pawn loses its support. [%cal Gc5d4] }
4. c3 { Gives d4 extra support. } 4... Nc6 { Adds a second attacker on d4. }
5. Nf3 { Defends d4 again and develops. } 5... Qb6 { A third attacker on d4, and the queen also eyes the b2 pawn. [%cal Gb6d4,Gc6d4] }
6. a3 { Prepares b4 to win space on the queenside. } ( 6. Be2 cxd4 7. cxd4 Nge7 8. Nc3 Nf5 ) 6... c4 { Stops b4 and keeps the queenside closed. The pawn also covers d3, so White's bishop cannot use that square. }
7. Nbd2 { Develops the knight. It cannot use b3, because the c4 pawn now covers that square. } 7... Na5 { Supports the c4 pawn and covers b3. }
8. Be2 { Develops the bishop and prepares castling. } 8... Bd7 { Brings out the bishop that was shut in behind the e6 pawn. }
9. O-O Ne7 { The knight heads for f5, where it can attack d4 again. } 10. Re1 Nf5 { Adds one more attacker to d4 and sits on a safe square. } *
